Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.560 position:63%
After years of trying, the tech industry
is finally making robots happen. From

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.039 position:58%
vacuuming to mowing to serving drinks
and patrolling airports.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:11.820 position:61%
These autonomous droids are everywhere.
And yes, they're a little creepy.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.880
But then there's this little guy,
the Gitamini.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.760
It's designed and programmed to be
paired with a human.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:22.890 position:64%
Sort of like a very obedient dog full of
ones and zeros. It also carries stuff for

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:25.410 position:66% line:92%
you, 20 pounds of stuff, making it a proxy

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:28.320 position:59%
backpack or kind of like a grocery bag
on wheels.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.950
If you trace Gita's family tree,
eventually you arrive at the Vespa.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.870 position:63%
A few years ago, Piaggio, the Italian
scooter giant, was looking for a product

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:40.850 position:63%
to crack the American market, which
never really warmed up to the Vespa. And

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.740 position:73% line:92%
invested in a Boston startup called FastForward

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:47.010
and the Gita project was born.
According to CEO Greg Lynn,

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:51.420 position:63%
the idea was to zig where other robot
startups were zagging. Instead of trying

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.620 position:59%
to replace the human entirely,
they set out to augment one. The Gita,

00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:00.300 position:64%
like a Vespa, was intended to replace car
trips, but by enabling walkable errands,

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.640 position:61%
say going to the corner store for a bag
of dog food.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:06.330 position:56%
The bot's good for the person, and
indirectly it's good for the planet.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.540 position:61%
Still, these aren't the droids a lot of
people are looking for.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.960 position:61%
Piaggio hasn't said how many they've
sold, and they've acknowledged that the

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:20.340 position:66% line:92%
Gita at ,850 has yet to really take over a

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:23.940
city or a whole neighborhood.
The larger opportunity lies in

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:27.690
commercial applications.
The company is now shifting to B2B

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:32.460 position:63%
and trying to sell to airports,
construction sites, industrial areas and

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:35.430 position:58%
clients like that.
Basically, anywhere you see a cart is

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:39.180 position:63%
is ripe terrain for a Gita. When palling
around with a Gita, you're sure to

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:42.300 position:56%
